1
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:11,800
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:32,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,333
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:41,233
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,467 --> 00:00:44,100
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:45,367
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,367 --> 00:00:46,700
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:47,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:51,333
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,467 --> 00:00:53,500
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:55,667
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:57,733
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,600
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,367 --> 00:01:02,833
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,267 --> 00:01:06,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,233 --> 00:01:11,867
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,867 --> 00:01:13,467
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,467 --> 00:01:15,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,033 --> 00:01:21,667
<i> We only found her jacket.</i>

21
00:01:21,667 --> 00:01:23,633
<i>Did you find her corpse?
You didn't.</i>

22
00:01:23,633 --> 00:01:25,367
<i>This is the floor plan
of the safe house.</i>

23
00:01:25,367 --> 00:01:27,700
<i> That place is heavily guarded.</i>

24
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:29,667
<i>- Boss, there's CCTV.
- Shut it down!</i>

25
00:01:30,567 --> 00:01:32,833
<i>- Did you catch them?
- They got away!</i>

26
00:01:32,833 --> 00:01:34,467
<i>Check the CCTV
at the safe house!</i>

27
00:01:34,467 --> 00:01:35,967
<i> You think you can fool me?</i>

28
00:01:35,967 --> 00:01:37,500
<i>Put down the fork.
One million.</i>

29
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:39,000
<i>You just need to have
this document signed.</i>

30
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,533
<i>Uh, Ma'am Betchay,
the applicants are here.</i>

31
00:01:40,567 --> 00:01:41,767
<i>- How old is she?
- Fifteen.</i>

32
00:01:41,767 --> 00:01:43,000
<i> Minors aren't allowed here.</i>

33
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,600
Ready? Present yourself elegant.

34
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:48,333
<i> Decent. Professional.</i>

35
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:50,333
<i> Oh!</i>

36
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:52,500
Hey, what was that?

37
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,500
Didn't you say I was
supposed to look formal?

38
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:00,000
- [MAMENG] Oh, no.
- There, this is formal.

39
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,500
That's not formal.

40
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:03,000
You look like you're
about to pick a fight.

41
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,933
Of course,
it should be like this.

42
00:02:04,933 --> 00:02:07,500
So they'll know
I'm always ready.

43
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:10,567
[RUDY] Son, you look like you're
more than ready to kill someone.

44
00:02:13,367 --> 00:02:17,867
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

45
00:02:19,067 --> 00:02:20,600
Go back! That's wrong.

46
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:21,933
Again, again!

47
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:23,967
- What am I supposed to do?
- You have to look decent!

48
00:02:23,967 --> 00:02:25,933
You're applying for a job!

49
00:02:25,933 --> 00:02:27,500
But I look decent, right?

50
00:02:27,567 --> 00:02:28,867
- Come on.
- Go on, son.

51
00:02:28,867 --> 00:02:31,600
- Should I walk slowly?
- Yes. Formal.

52
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:32,933
Am I supposed to look friendly?

53
00:02:32,933 --> 00:02:34,333
Of course!

54
00:02:34,933 --> 00:02:36,967
- Just do what she says.
- Come on.

55
00:02:36,967 --> 00:02:38,600
- Son.
- Tsk.

56
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,067
- [RUDY] He's just excited.
- [HUFFS]

57
00:02:41,067 --> 00:02:42,933
- He can do it.
- He's probably just excited.

58
00:02:42,933 --> 00:02:44,600
Maybe he was just too excited.

59
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:47,767
[GABO YELLING]

60
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:48,967
- I'm ready!
- He's ready.

61
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:59,933
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

62
00:03:06,667 --> 00:03:07,733
Good morning.

63
00:03:07,733 --> 00:03:10,833
[LAUGHTER]

64
00:03:10,833 --> 00:03:12,400
Good morning, ma'am.

65
00:03:13,633 --> 00:03:15,333
- (In Japanese) Hello.
- Hey.

66
00:03:15,333 --> 00:03:16,733
Good morning.

67
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:18,800
- [MAMENG CHUCKLING]
- That'll do.

68
00:03:19,633 --> 00:03:20,967
You may take your seat.

69
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,600
Nice! Nice!

70
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,367
[GABO CHUCKLES]

71
00:03:24,367 --> 00:03:25,767
I guess this is easy!

72
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,733
- Hey!
- What?

73
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:33,733
Fix your posture.
Not like that!

74
00:03:34,033 --> 00:03:35,633
This is fine!

75
00:03:35,633 --> 00:03:36,967
Sit up straight.

76
00:03:37,033 --> 00:03:38,633
- Just relax.
- Relax?

77
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:41,667
That looks relaxed.

78
00:03:41,667 --> 00:03:43,700
Gabo, you're applying for a job,

79
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:45,967
not relaxing at home.

80
00:03:45,967 --> 00:03:47,833
Fix your posture!

81
00:03:47,833 --> 00:03:49,667
How am I supposed
to relax, Aunty?

82
00:03:49,667 --> 00:03:51,600
Look presentable,
but stay relaxed.

83
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:53,433
How? Like this?

84
00:03:53,433 --> 00:03:55,600
Fix it.
You're applying for a job.

85
00:03:55,633 --> 00:03:57,000
Put your hands here.

86
00:03:58,033 --> 00:03:59,200
- There.
- Like this?

87
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:00,533
Fix it. Like this!

88
00:04:00,533 --> 00:04:02,067
- There, keep it there.
- Like this?

89
00:04:02,067 --> 00:04:03,867
- Relax.
- There you go.

90
00:04:03,867 --> 00:04:05,167
- There.
- Okay.

91
00:04:05,167 --> 00:04:06,800
- Like this?
- Yes.

92
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,967
- Ready?
- Ready!

93
00:04:08,967 --> 00:04:10,500
Okay, we'll start.

94
00:04:11,467 --> 00:04:12,867
Tell me about yourself.

95
00:04:12,867 --> 00:04:16,033
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

96
00:04:16,033 --> 00:04:18,467
Why is everything in English?
I mean...

97
00:04:19,533 --> 00:04:21,833
We're in the Philippines, and...

98
00:04:22,867 --> 00:04:24,400
How am I supposed
to understand that?

99
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:26,633
Gabo, that's how
interviews are.

100
00:04:26,633 --> 00:04:28,567
They usually use English.

101
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,867
That's why we need
to practice now.

102
00:04:30,867 --> 00:04:32,667
- [MAMENG] Mm-hmm.
- Go ahead.

103
00:04:32,667 --> 00:04:34,733
Tell me about yourself.

104
00:04:34,733 --> 00:04:36,700
Well, um...

105
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:38,833
I have...

106
00:04:38,833 --> 00:04:42,700
I have two hands, two eyes,

107
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:44,133
one nose, and one lip.

108
00:04:45,067 --> 00:04:46,967
[CHUCKLES]

109
00:04:48,233 --> 00:04:50,100
Okay, I'll just move on
to the next question, Pa.

110
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:51,567
- [RUDY] Sure, sure.
- Okay, how about this?

111
00:04:51,567 --> 00:04:53,067
What are your strengths?

112
00:04:53,067 --> 00:04:54,733
Strengths?

113
00:04:54,733 --> 00:04:57,833
Your strengths.
What are you good at?

114
00:04:57,833 --> 00:04:59,067
- Strength?
- Yes.

115
00:04:59,067 --> 00:05:01,433
[LAUGHING] Am I strong?

116
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:03,100
I'm strong!

117
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,767
Very strong!

118
00:05:04,767 --> 00:05:06,067
I'm strong!

119
00:05:06,067 --> 00:05:07,567
[GABO CHUCKLING]

120
00:05:07,567 --> 00:05:10,867
I'm not asking about
physical strength.

121
00:05:10,867 --> 00:05:12,067
What are your skills?

122
00:05:12,067 --> 00:05:13,933
What can you do that
you think only you can do?

123
00:05:13,933 --> 00:05:15,567
What can you brag about?

124
00:05:15,633 --> 00:05:16,600
Oh...

125
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:18,567
I fight!

126
00:05:19,533 --> 00:05:20,700
Very fight!

127
00:05:21,133 --> 00:05:23,067
I can fight many people!

128
00:05:23,133 --> 00:05:24,933
Okay, let's try that again.

129
00:05:24,933 --> 00:05:27,567
Let's try this one.

130
00:05:27,567 --> 00:05:30,067
What's your greatest weakness?

131
00:05:30,067 --> 00:05:32,700
Aunty, what's a weakness?
What does that mean?

132
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:35,200
It means your biggest weakness.

133
00:05:37,167 --> 00:05:38,933
I know that one!

134
00:05:39,767 --> 00:05:41,100
My weakness...

135
00:05:42,067 --> 00:05:43,167
is my wife.

136
00:05:43,167 --> 00:05:44,633
Hey, hey!

137
00:05:44,633 --> 00:05:46,733
That's the perfect answer.

138
00:05:47,167 --> 00:05:50,100
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

139
00:05:56,133 --> 00:05:57,533
Because...

140
00:05:58,067 --> 00:06:01,067
when my wife tells me
to do something, I obey.

141
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,100
- [DANTE] That's it!
- [RUDY] That works.

142
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:06,633
[GABO CHUCKLING]

143
00:06:06,633 --> 00:06:09,033
[SAM] <i>   I wonder if this guy
</i> can actually get a job.

144
00:06:11,167 --> 00:06:14,233
Agent Tuazon, I'm going
to need a copy of your report.

145
00:06:16,933 --> 00:06:19,633
Yes, Colonel.
I'll send it to your office.

146
00:06:19,633 --> 00:06:22,167
Your agency is quite good at
making things look intentional,

147
00:06:22,167 --> 00:06:23,800
Fernando.

148
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,267
What is this?
Are you proud that

149
00:06:25,267 --> 00:06:27,300
you were the first
to find out...

150
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,133
that Samantha Jacinto
was dead?

151
00:06:31,667 --> 00:06:34,833
We're not proud that
we were the first to learn

152
00:06:34,833 --> 00:06:36,533
about Sam's death.

153
00:06:36,533 --> 00:06:37,800
So, what is it then?

154
00:06:38,033 --> 00:06:39,533
Guilt?

155
00:06:39,533 --> 00:06:42,133
Because you know your
incompetence had something to do

156
00:06:42,167 --> 00:06:45,000
with Samantha Jacinto's death?

157
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
- What are you trying to imply?
- Colonel.

158
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:54,000
A major syndicate went up
against the NCIA.

159
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,333
And all of us here prepared
for that.

160
00:06:57,167 --> 00:07:00,000
We just didn't expect things
to turn out this way.

161
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:04,033
You didn't expect it because
of your incompetence.

162
00:07:04,033 --> 00:07:05,667
That's my whole point.

163
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,833
And that's all I have to say...

164
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,667
...for now.

165
00:07:13,167 --> 00:07:20,000
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

166
00:07:28,333 --> 00:07:29,567
[MUSIC STOPS]

167
00:07:30,067 --> 00:07:37,000
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

168
00:07:42,167 --> 00:07:44,233
- [ISOBEL SOBBING]
- [MAXINE] Mom.

169
00:07:44,233 --> 00:07:45,400
Mom.

170
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:47,033
[GRUNTS] Dear...

171
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:50,900
Director Delgado
dropped by earlier.

172
00:07:50,900 --> 00:07:52,367
- I know.
- [ISOBEL SOBS]

173
00:07:52,367 --> 00:07:54,200
We held a meeting with him
at the NCIA

174
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:55,900
because of the jacket that
was discovered, and we...

175
00:07:56,433 --> 00:07:58,833
We did a water search but...

176
00:08:00,433 --> 00:08:02,667
- There was no trace of Sam.
- No!

177
00:08:02,733 --> 00:08:06,133
Look for her in a drum
in Manila Bay!

178
00:08:06,133 --> 00:08:09,967
Your sister is there.
Believe me. [CRIES]

179
00:08:09,967 --> 00:08:11,067
[PINKY] She's right.

180
00:08:11,067 --> 00:08:14,300
That's what Madam Rosa said.

181
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:17,100
We should, at least, hold a
funeral and bury her.

182
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:20,033
That way, her soul can finally
rest in peace.

183
00:08:22,167 --> 00:08:24,233
[MAXINE] Sam is not dead.

184
00:08:24,233 --> 00:08:26,700
Sam is alive, Ma. She's alive!

185
00:08:26,967 --> 00:08:28,133
She is.

186
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:29,233
[BREATH QUIVERS]

187
00:08:29,233 --> 00:08:31,233
She's alive in my heart.

188
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:35,267
But we have to
accept the truth.

189
00:08:35,833 --> 00:08:37,967
We can't bring her back

190
00:08:37,967 --> 00:08:39,967
because your sister is dead.

191
00:08:40,067 --> 00:08:43,067
Trust me, she's dead.

192
00:08:43,067 --> 00:08:44,400
She's gone.

193
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:47,800
- [SOBS] Isobel...
- [SOBS] Pinky...

194
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:49,833
Pinky. [SOBBING]

195
00:08:49,833 --> 00:08:51,267
[PINKY] Be strong.

196
00:08:51,267 --> 00:08:53,733
[ISOBEL SOBBING]

197
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:58,100
[MAXINE BREATHING HEAVILY]

198
00:08:58,133 --> 00:09:05,100
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

199
00:09:05,933 --> 00:09:07,000
[MAXINE EXHALES DEEPLY]

200
00:09:14,833 --> 00:09:15,833
[MAXINE] Dad.

201
00:09:17,867 --> 00:09:19,233
You should take it easy.

202
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:28,000
I can't, Max.

203
00:09:33,967 --> 00:09:35,700
Your sister has left us.

204
00:09:41,867 --> 00:09:42,833
[RICARDO EXHALES DEEPLY]

205
00:09:46,833 --> 00:09:48,200
[GRUNTS, SNIFFLES]

206
00:09:50,167 --> 00:09:52,167
The heaven is punishing me
because...

207
00:09:54,167 --> 00:09:55,400
Because I'm a bad father.

208
00:09:55,400 --> 00:10:02,033
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

209
00:10:02,067 --> 00:10:03,033
Dad.

210
00:10:05,067 --> 00:10:07,133
You've been a good father to us.

211
00:10:13,833 --> 00:10:15,033
Not to Sam.

212
00:10:20,067 --> 00:10:22,833
Every single day,
I made her feel like...

213
00:10:24,233 --> 00:10:26,033
she didn't deserve to be loved.

214
00:10:28,433 --> 00:10:30,067
That she should've been
the one who died

215
00:10:31,067 --> 00:10:32,400
instead of her brother.

216
00:10:36,567 --> 00:10:38,400
I was so unfair to Sam.

217
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:43,167
But that's because I...

218
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:48,267
I didn't know how to deal
with my career.

219
00:10:50,233 --> 00:10:51,233
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

220
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:54,100
Now...

221
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:57,333
I'm going to mourn two of
my children every day.

222
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:03,033
The loss of my two children.

223
00:11:06,933 --> 00:11:10,167
[SOBBING]

224
00:11:11,467 --> 00:11:14,033
I'm not just carrying
a heavy weight.

225
00:11:17,967 --> 00:11:20,100
This feels like...

226
00:11:21,433 --> 00:11:22,533
falling,

227
00:11:24,133 --> 00:11:25,133
being left...

228
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:31,267
and abandoned in hell.

229
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:34,467
[SOBS]

230
00:11:34,467 --> 00:11:41,433
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

231
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:57,433
I'm so sorry, Isobel.

232
00:11:57,433 --> 00:12:01,800
I can't be in Sam's
memorial service tomorrow.

233
00:12:02,767 --> 00:12:05,800
[SNIFFLES] I have something
important to take care of

234
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:06,800
in Switzerland.

235
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,000
No problem.

236
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,267
I can hear her saying,
"Auntie Pinky,

237
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:17,567
I don't want to get in the way
of your commitments."

238
00:12:17,567 --> 00:12:20,000
That's exactly
how I remember Sam.

239
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:24,533
She's always very understanding.

240
00:12:25,367 --> 00:12:27,500
[VOICE BREAKING]
If only there's a way to know

241
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:29,967
what my daughter
wants to tell me.

242
00:12:31,633 --> 00:12:32,700
Isobel,

243
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:37,367
can I give your number
to Madam Rosa?

244
00:12:37,367 --> 00:12:39,667
She can sense

245
00:12:39,667 --> 00:12:42,800
when you'd need her the most.

246
00:12:43,533 --> 00:12:45,700
She'll call you.

247
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:48,133
Is that okay?

248
00:12:48,167 --> 00:12:50,000
[VOICE SHAKING] Yes, please.

249
00:12:50,833 --> 00:12:52,833
My condolences, Isobel. [SOBS]

250
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:56,500
- [PINKY SNIFFLES]
- Thank you, Pinky.

251
00:12:57,100 --> 00:12:58,067
Thank you.

252
00:12:59,533 --> 00:13:02,600
Isobel, you better rest.
Get some sleep.

253
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:04,000
[SOFTLY] Yeah.

254
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,400
I'll head out.

255
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:06,167
Okay.

256
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,467
[DOOR OPENS]

257
00:13:14,833 --> 00:13:15,967
[DOOR CLOSES]

258
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:20,867
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

259
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:22,667
It's okay. [SOBS, SNIFFLES]

260
00:13:25,867 --> 00:13:29,500
[SOBBING, SNIFFLING CONTINUES]

261
00:13:32,433 --> 00:13:34,867
This is everything
you ever wanted.

262
00:13:37,967 --> 00:13:39,200
For Sam to be gone.

263
00:13:41,867 --> 00:13:43,467
Are you happy now?

264
00:13:43,467 --> 00:13:44,833
How can you say that?

265
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:47,967
I am a father
who lost my daughter.

266
00:13:47,967 --> 00:13:51,100
You weren't a dad to Sam
for a long time.

267
00:13:52,067 --> 00:13:53,633
[CHAIR DRAGS]

268
00:13:53,633 --> 00:13:54,600
Please.

269
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,700
This is more painful for me

270
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:03,100
because I know
I wasn't there for her.

271
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:04,067
I didn't forget that.

272
00:14:05,633 --> 00:14:07,800
It's a mistake
I can do nothing about now.

273
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:08,733
You're right.

274
00:14:09,967 --> 00:14:11,800
You can do nothing now.

275
00:14:13,733 --> 00:14:17,000
Those countless days
of making her feel

276
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,067
undeserving of love

277
00:14:19,067 --> 00:14:21,000
until your last moments
with her,

278
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,967
that's what you made her feel!

279
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,900
We don't know for sure,

280
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:28,233
maybe while she was dying,

281
00:14:28,267 --> 00:14:30,567
she still looked for you. "Dad!"

282
00:14:31,867 --> 00:14:33,667
[SOBBING] "Please help me!"

283
00:14:34,667 --> 00:14:35,800
"Where are you?"

284
00:14:38,267 --> 00:14:40,733
But you were never there.

285
00:14:45,667 --> 00:14:46,800
[ISOBEL HUFFS]

286
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:48,767
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

287
00:14:48,767 --> 00:14:53,700
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

288
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:54,667
Sir.

289
00:14:56,867 --> 00:14:58,000
I'm sorry.

290
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,600
Sorry for what?

291
00:15:01,667 --> 00:15:05,267
It was my idea to keep
our findings from NLEA.

292
00:15:06,133 --> 00:15:09,167
Now they're taking shots at us.

293
00:15:10,033 --> 00:15:11,500
You know what, Sebastian,

294
00:15:12,533 --> 00:15:14,167
Domingo's right.

295
00:15:14,167 --> 00:15:16,633
My conscience is haunting me.

296
00:15:17,533 --> 00:15:20,300
Maybe it's half my fault
that Sam's gone.

297
00:15:21,167 --> 00:15:27,233
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

298
00:15:27,233 --> 00:15:29,800
You made me look bad, Fernando.

299
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:33,000
<i> I'll do you even worse.</i>

300
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,700
<i> I'm going to prove to everyone</i>

301
00:15:34,700 --> 00:15:37,900
that NCIA agents are incompetent

302
00:15:37,933 --> 00:15:40,333
<i> put next to NLEA.</i>

303
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:44,700
[DOOR OPENS]

304
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:47,233
Sir.

305
00:15:47,233 --> 00:15:48,833
There's something
you need to know.

306
00:15:48,833 --> 00:15:49,867
What is it?

307
00:15:49,867 --> 00:15:52,567
When you were in NCIA,

308
00:15:53,567 --> 00:15:57,900
there was intel that the safe
house where we're keeping

309
00:15:57,900 --> 00:16:00,767
the gold bars owned by
the Zafra's was broken into.

310
00:16:00,767 --> 00:16:02,833
NLEA was alerted and went there.

311
00:16:02,833 --> 00:16:04,533
Unfortunately,
the suspects got away.

312
00:16:05,367 --> 00:16:07,233
What the-- [SLAMS TABLE]

313
00:16:07,233 --> 00:16:08,933
It's already in your custody,

314
00:16:08,967 --> 00:16:11,233
and the criminals
still got away with it?

315
00:16:11,233 --> 00:16:13,800
Sir, they didn't plan on
giving up on those gold bars.

316
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:15,767
We immediately went
to Ginintuang Lupa.

317
00:16:15,767 --> 00:16:17,333
They said that's where
the suspect headed.

318
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:23,067
Tell me that you
at least identified who did it.

319
00:16:23,067 --> 00:16:24,733
Hmm?

320
00:16:24,733 --> 00:16:25,733
What?

321
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:27,733
Nothing? [SLAMS TABLE]

322
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:30,067
Sir, we think it's still the men

323
00:16:30,067 --> 00:16:32,767
who were responsible
for the first encounter.

324
00:16:32,767 --> 00:16:35,600
I won't inform General Jacinto
about this for now.

325
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:36,933
Just until I can.

326
00:16:36,933 --> 00:16:39,067
NLEA isn't looking good
for him right now.

327
00:16:39,067 --> 00:16:40,100
Why, sir?

328
00:16:40,100 --> 00:16:42,233
His daughter is dead.

329
00:16:42,267 --> 00:16:45,633
The NCIA found Sam's jacket
riddled with bullets.

330
00:16:45,633 --> 00:16:48,167
But her body is yet to be found.

331
00:16:48,167 --> 00:16:49,333
Which means

332
00:16:49,333 --> 00:16:51,133
we can't add more problems

333
00:16:51,133 --> 00:16:54,933
that'll make us look bad
in General Jacinto's eyes.

334
00:16:55,833 --> 00:16:57,000
Do you understand?

335
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:57,933
Yes, sir.

336
00:16:58,933 --> 00:16:59,933
Yes, sir.

337
00:17:00,767 --> 00:17:02,267
Okay. This one.

338
00:17:03,267 --> 00:17:06,400
If you are put
in a difficult situation,

339
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:07,367
what will you do?

340
00:17:12,233 --> 00:17:14,767
Y-You can say pass. Go. Say it.

341
00:17:15,467 --> 00:17:16,967
What does that mean, Auntie?

342
00:17:16,967 --> 00:17:18,933
[ALL CHUCKLING]

343
00:17:18,933 --> 00:17:21,800
If you've been put
in a tight spot,

344
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:23,833
how will you think
you'll handle it?

345
00:17:23,833 --> 00:17:25,000
I...

346
00:17:25,700 --> 00:17:26,667
I think...

347
00:17:26,667 --> 00:17:28,000
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

348
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,367
of what can be... the solution.

349
00:17:30,367 --> 00:17:33,267
I-I think, uh...

350
00:17:34,467 --> 00:17:35,800
possibly--

351
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:37,833
- [DANTE] Okay...
- Positive!

352
00:17:39,133 --> 00:17:40,733
To...

353
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:42,833
to...

354
00:17:42,833 --> 00:17:46,133
to give the solution
of any problem!

355
00:17:46,133 --> 00:17:48,967
I need to... protect

356
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,400
my constituents!

357
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:51,800
- Nice!
- Ooh!

358
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:52,800
[RUDY, DANTE CHUCKLE]

359
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:54,867
Many people-- I protect!

360
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:57,233
- And I say...
- That's beautiful.

361
00:17:57,233 --> 00:17:59,167
- ...this is my priority!

362
00:17:59,167 --> 00:18:00,167
- Yes!
- Good one!

363
00:18:00,167 --> 00:18:01,400
More than anything else!

364
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:03,133
- Yes!
- Nice one! [CLAPS]

365
00:18:03,133 --> 00:18:04,333
- Long live! Long live!
- [GABO LAUGHS]

366
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:05,700
- Long live!
- Was that good?

367
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:07,833
That's like
a Miss Universe answer!

368
00:18:07,833 --> 00:18:09,033
That's like
a Miss Universe answer! [CLAPS]

369
00:18:09,033 --> 00:18:10,867
That's easy-peasy!
[LAUGHS]

370
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,900
Okay. Last question.

371
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:15,267
I can answer that!

372
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:18,000
Why should we hire you?

373
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,233
Oh.

374
00:18:20,233 --> 00:18:21,200
Why?

375
00:18:24,033 --> 00:18:26,867
- That's hard.
- Why should we get you?

376
00:18:26,867 --> 00:18:27,867
- That's it!
- That's it!

377
00:18:27,867 --> 00:18:28,833
Uh...

378
00:18:30,533 --> 00:18:31,700
because...

379
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,367
Because I applied!

380
00:18:34,367 --> 00:18:35,333
[RUDY] Yes! Right! Right!

381
00:18:35,333 --> 00:18:36,533
I applied.

382
00:18:36,533 --> 00:18:39,033
- [MAMENG] That's right!
- You need me!

383
00:18:39,033 --> 00:18:41,000
You need an employee!

384
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,533
- [MAMENG] Yes.
- So I applied!

385
00:18:42,533 --> 00:18:45,333
[LAUGHTER]

386
00:18:45,333 --> 00:18:46,900
I need a job

387
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:48,200
so I applied.

388
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:49,400
You need a worker.

389
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:51,033
Good enough.

390
00:18:51,033 --> 00:18:52,367
I think this is okay. [CHUCKLES]

391
00:18:52,367 --> 00:18:54,167
We're all good here.

392
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:56,367
No other questions, ma'am?

393
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:58,400
No.

394
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:00,433
Thank you. You may go.

395
00:19:00,433 --> 00:19:02,200
I-I passed?

396
00:19:03,233 --> 00:19:04,767
What do you guys think?
Did he pass?

397
00:19:04,767 --> 00:19:07,200
He gave a very
Miss Universe kind of answer.

398
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,433
Did I pass, ma'am?

399
00:19:08,433 --> 00:19:09,900
It's good enough, I guess.

400
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:11,433
- She said it's good.
- You'll be fine.

401
00:19:11,433 --> 00:19:13,000
I'll go home.

402
00:19:14,233 --> 00:19:15,533
Thank you so much, maam.

403
00:19:15,533 --> 00:19:18,300
And, uh, nice meeting you.

404
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:20,067
[MUSIC TURNS SOFT]

405
00:19:20,067 --> 00:19:21,433
Good morning.

406
00:19:21,433 --> 00:19:23,400
And see you soon.

407
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,100
[DANTE] Oh, wow.

408
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:26,167
[SOFT SMOOCH]

409
00:19:29,433 --> 00:19:30,867
Nice, nice.

410
00:19:32,167 --> 00:19:33,833
- Nice one.
- Great. Nice one.

411
00:19:33,833 --> 00:19:35,067
- I need to go.
- Yes.

412
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,967
My son just went out.

413
00:19:37,967 --> 00:19:40,267
[LAUGHTER]

414
00:19:40,267 --> 00:19:42,400
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

415
00:19:48,667 --> 00:19:51,633
[BOTTLE CLANGS]

416
00:19:54,467 --> 00:19:55,433
[BOTTLE THUDS]

417
00:19:59,467 --> 00:20:01,767
- [GLASS THUDS]
- [ALCOHOL POURING]

418
00:20:02,667 --> 00:20:09,633
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

419
00:20:11,300 --> 00:20:12,300
[PIA] Sir?

420
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:15,767
- [GLASS THUDS]
- [FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

421
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:18,167
[BOTTLE THUDS]

422
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:22,733
I'm sorry.

423
00:20:26,367 --> 00:20:27,567
[CLEARS THROAT]

424
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:35,700
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

425
00:20:35,733 --> 00:20:36,867
Sir, it's okay.

426
00:20:38,067 --> 00:20:42,033
You don't have to hide it.
I understand you.

427
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:45,333
I know how you feel.

428
00:20:45,333 --> 00:20:47,633
Sometimes,
that's what we really need.

429
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:52,633
Sir,
now that we're one man down...

430
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:54,300
What are our plans?

431
00:20:55,067 --> 00:20:56,833
Will we go through
a restructuring?

432
00:20:56,833 --> 00:20:59,033
Sir, I'm sorry...

433
00:21:00,033 --> 00:21:03,167
...if I seem to be in a rush.

434
00:21:03,167 --> 00:21:07,800
However, evil does not rest.

435
00:21:11,767 --> 00:21:14,200
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

436
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:15,167
You're right.

437
00:21:17,267 --> 00:21:22,367
As the NCIA, we must not stop
from working.

438
00:21:22,367 --> 00:21:27,667
However, I will allow my team
and give them time to grieve.

439
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:30,167
I understand.

440
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:35,067
If you need me,
I'm just right here.

441
00:21:35,767 --> 00:21:42,733
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

442
00:21:57,767 --> 00:22:04,767
[UNSETTLING MUSIC
CONTINUES, FADES]

443
00:22:05,300 --> 00:22:06,267
[GLASS THUDS]

444
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,400
[BOTTLE CLINKS]

445
00:22:11,300 --> 00:22:12,333
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

446
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:17,300
- [LINE RINGING]
- [PHONE RINGS]

447
00:22:18,500 --> 00:22:19,467
[RICARDO]  Domingo.

448
00:22:19,467 --> 00:22:20,800
[DOMINGO]  Gen. Jacinto.

449
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:24,133
I know the NCIA could not find
Sam's body.

450
00:22:24,133 --> 00:22:26,167
<i>I want you to go
to Ginintuang Lupa,</i>

451
00:22:26,167 --> 00:22:27,433
and look for leads.

452
00:22:28,333 --> 00:22:30,900
Look for leads for what, sir?

453
00:22:30,967 --> 00:22:33,000
Leads on what happened
to my daughter!

454
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:35,100
<i>At the very least,
I want to find...</i>

455
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:37,133
...Sam's corpse.

456
00:22:37,133 --> 00:22:39,000
<i> Mobilize your people.</i>

457
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:40,967
Do something useful for once!

458
00:22:40,967 --> 00:22:44,100
- Yes, Gen. Jacinto.
- [LINE DROPS]

459
00:22:52,367 --> 00:22:56,800
[IMITATING A BOXER]

460
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:59,333
So, love?
Were my answers good?

461
00:22:59,333 --> 00:23:03,367
- They are, right?
- They'll suffice.

462
00:23:03,367 --> 00:23:06,200
Tomorrow, don't forget
everything I told you

463
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:09,033
about how to answer,
and how to sit.

464
00:23:09,033 --> 00:23:11,167
And don't forget your clothes.

465
00:23:11,167 --> 00:23:15,000
Love, don't worry about it.
I'll ace this!

466
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:17,000
You know what
I'm worried about tomorrow?

467
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:19,033
Several companies might chase
after me!

468
00:23:19,033 --> 00:23:20,333
I wouldn't even know
which to pick!

469
00:23:20,933 --> 00:23:23,000
Okay, I'll pray for you.

470
00:23:24,833 --> 00:23:25,800
Uh...

471
00:23:26,233 --> 00:23:29,133
Love, I think we better...

472
00:23:30,333 --> 00:23:32,233
...sleep right away.

473
00:23:32,233 --> 00:23:35,967
I'll be leaving early tomorrow,
so I could be first in line.

474
00:23:35,967 --> 00:23:38,400
No one can definitely go
before me.

475
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:40,800
[BOTH CHUCKLING SOFTLY]

476
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:43,133
I hope...

477
00:23:45,533 --> 00:23:46,800
I can get a job.

478
00:23:47,567 --> 00:23:49,300
I wish I could get a good job.

479
00:23:50,333 --> 00:23:52,133
My dream really is...

480
00:23:53,500 --> 00:23:55,100
...to be able
to help my family.

481
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:58,200
Especially now.

482
00:23:59,833 --> 00:24:00,900
'Cause you're here.

483
00:24:01,900 --> 00:24:03,833
When we have a child,
I want...

484
00:24:04,400 --> 00:24:05,600
...to have a proper job.

485
00:24:05,600 --> 00:24:08,600
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

486
00:24:08,600 --> 00:24:10,233
Don't worry.

487
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:14,067
Your heart is
in the right place.

488
00:24:14,867 --> 00:24:18,067
And God sees
what is truly in our hearts.

489
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:21,133
[GABO BREATHES DEEPLY]

490
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:22,800
What about you, love?

491
00:24:23,567 --> 00:24:25,067
Can you see...

492
00:24:26,500 --> 00:24:28,000
..what's in my heart?

493
00:24:29,267 --> 00:24:30,600
What's on my mind?

494
00:24:31,600 --> 00:24:33,267
What's on my eyes?

495
00:24:34,233 --> 00:24:35,200
Because...

496
00:24:36,900 --> 00:24:38,200
I'll finally get a job.

497
00:24:38,967 --> 00:24:40,267
I'll receive a bigger pay.

498
00:24:41,133 --> 00:24:43,367
I'll be able to fulfill
all my dreams.

499
00:24:44,133 --> 00:24:45,567
All that's left is for us
to have a child.

500
00:24:47,267 --> 00:24:48,867
If we could...

501
00:24:49,433 --> 00:24:52,500
...why don't we start a family?
Make a baby?

502
00:24:53,133 --> 00:24:56,433
So when I get my first paycheck,
I already know what to buy.

503
00:24:57,467 --> 00:24:59,900
I'll buy necessary things
for our child,

504
00:24:59,900 --> 00:25:01,600
and I'll save up
for their education.

505
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:05,433
You have to be up early
tomorrow, right?

506
00:25:05,433 --> 00:25:07,400
Come on, let's go to sleep.

507
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:10,633
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

508
00:25:10,633 --> 00:25:11,633
Love.

509
00:25:12,333 --> 00:25:15,400
Why don't you think about it?

510
00:25:15,400 --> 00:25:16,467
Because...

511
00:25:17,267 --> 00:25:18,600
We shouldn't waste
too much time.

512
00:25:19,433 --> 00:25:23,567
Wouldn't it be better
if I'm working and saving money

513
00:25:23,567 --> 00:25:25,233
as our child grows?

514
00:25:25,233 --> 00:25:26,500
[SAM CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

515
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:28,133
You have a lot of plans,
don't you?

516
00:25:28,133 --> 00:25:29,333
- Huh?
- Hm?

517
00:25:29,333 --> 00:25:31,433
Get your first paycheck first.

518
00:25:32,300 --> 00:25:33,567
But love...

519
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:36,900
When I get my first paycheck,

520
00:25:36,933 --> 00:25:40,233
you should give me
a reward.

521
00:25:40,700 --> 00:25:43,600
And when I get home from work,
I want you...

522
00:25:44,333 --> 00:25:47,667
...to be freshly bathed.
You'll smell so good.

523
00:25:47,667 --> 00:25:49,967
I'll take a bath
when I get home, too.

524
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:54,300
Then you'll give me a massage
'cause I'm so exhausted.

525
00:25:54,300 --> 00:25:55,667
Wouldn't that be nice?

526
00:25:57,200 --> 00:25:59,500
Ah, it's so fun to dream.

527
00:26:00,467 --> 00:26:02,500
I'm so excited to go
to work tomorrow.

528
00:26:03,633 --> 00:26:05,467
- [SANTOS] Sir.
- Hm?

529
00:26:05,467 --> 00:26:07,967
This is the CCTV footage
of the safe house.

530
00:26:07,967 --> 00:26:14,900
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

531
00:26:16,500 --> 00:26:18,200
[KEYBOARD CLACKS]

532
00:26:21,300 --> 00:26:23,667
That damn bastard.
Who are you?

533
00:26:24,567 --> 00:26:26,200
Damn it.

534
00:26:26,300 --> 00:26:29,133
You can't hide from me
for the rest of your life.

535
00:26:29,967 --> 00:26:31,400
Sir.

536
00:26:31,400 --> 00:26:35,467
Why didn't we tell the colonel
about this new guy?

537
00:26:37,333 --> 00:26:39,067
Don't worry about the colonel.

538
00:26:39,067 --> 00:26:44,333
We'll just surprise him
when we catch this jerk.

539
00:26:45,067 --> 00:26:52,000
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

540
00:26:55,500 --> 00:26:56,800
[MAN] I'm glad
we got to vote about it,

541
00:26:57,700 --> 00:26:59,100
and that Mister Rudy won.

542
00:26:59,100 --> 00:27:00,167
Yeah.

543
00:27:00,167 --> 00:27:01,600
I'm glad, too.

544
00:27:01,600 --> 00:27:04,133
Otherwise, we would've
lost our homes by now.

545
00:27:04,767 --> 00:27:07,000
Simang, give me
two one-liter beers.

546
00:27:07,933 --> 00:27:09,467
Sure, wait a second.

547
00:27:11,433 --> 00:27:12,367
Oh.

548
00:27:14,567 --> 00:27:15,333
Here.

549
00:27:15,633 --> 00:27:16,600
Here you go.

550
00:27:16,600 --> 00:27:17,933
I'll get my change back
tomorrow.

551
00:27:17,933 --> 00:27:18,900
[SIMANG] Alright.

552
00:27:18,900 --> 00:27:20,000
Miss Betchay.

553
00:27:20,633 --> 00:27:21,867
That's a lot of money you got.

554
00:27:21,867 --> 00:27:23,700
Did you sign the document?

555
00:27:23,700 --> 00:27:25,533
[SCOFFS]

556
00:27:25,533 --> 00:27:27,600
I don't have to sign
to get a lot of money.

557
00:27:27,600 --> 00:27:29,867
I have a job, unlike you bums.

558
00:27:30,700 --> 00:27:31,600
Besides,

559
00:27:31,600 --> 00:27:34,433
why's it matter if I did sign?

560
00:27:34,433 --> 00:27:37,867
I can't pass up the opportunity
to have a lot of money.

561
00:27:37,867 --> 00:27:39,667
But we might lose
our homes, Betchay.

562
00:27:39,933 --> 00:27:41,433
[CHUCKLES]

563
00:27:41,433 --> 00:27:43,733
Do you think not signing it
would save your house?

564
00:27:43,733 --> 00:27:45,767
Do you really own
the land you have now?

565
00:27:46,067 --> 00:27:47,067
Of course, not.

566
00:27:47,067 --> 00:27:48,967
Why would you waste
your lives here?

567
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:51,067
Do you really want to rot
in this place?

568
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:54,600
If you're being offered
a huge sum of money,

569
00:27:54,667 --> 00:27:57,800
why shouldn't you take it?

570
00:27:57,800 --> 00:28:00,033
Wouldn't you want
to use it to start a new life?

571
00:28:00,900 --> 00:28:03,767
Oh, come on.
Stop lying to yourselves.

572
00:28:04,100 --> 00:28:07,733
We all grew up here.
I know you'd do the same.

573
00:28:08,067 --> 00:28:09,900
We all want some easy money.

574
00:28:09,900 --> 00:28:11,100
Well...

575
00:28:11,100 --> 00:28:13,400
Betchay has a point.

576
00:28:18,967 --> 00:28:25,933
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

577
00:28:40,933 --> 00:28:47,900
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

578
00:28:54,100 --> 00:28:56,767
[BEER POURING]

579
00:29:03,133 --> 00:29:10,100
[MUSIC TURNS PENSIVE]

580
00:29:19,633 --> 00:29:24,100
[BETCHAY]  What should I do
to make Rudy sign?

581
00:29:26,167 --> 00:29:28,267
<i> Should I really do this?</i>

582
00:29:30,100 --> 00:29:32,033
<i> But...</i>

583
00:29:32,033 --> 00:29:36,067
<i>that one million pesos
could change my life.</i>

584
00:29:38,100 --> 00:29:42,167
<i>I can finally get away
from this place.</i>

585
00:29:44,167 --> 00:29:46,867
<i> But how about the neighbors?</i>

586
00:29:48,267 --> 00:29:49,567
<i> Oh, well.</i>

587
00:29:50,267 --> 00:29:52,833
<i>They don't care about me,
anyway.</i>

588
00:29:52,833 --> 00:29:55,900
<i>Since they already see me
as a bad person,</i>

589
00:29:56,233 --> 00:29:58,567
<i>I'll show them
just how evil I can be.</i>

590
00:30:01,167 --> 00:30:02,133
[GLASS THUDS]

591
00:30:04,600 --> 00:30:05,533
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

592
00:30:09,300 --> 00:30:11,867
Oh, Gloria...

593
00:30:11,867 --> 00:30:18,833
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

594
00:30:24,767 --> 00:30:26,867
[GIBO]
<i> I'm sorry for lying to you.</i>

595
00:30:29,367 --> 00:30:32,167
<i>I just can't tell you
about my mission.</i>

596
00:30:34,100 --> 00:30:36,667
<i>I hope one day
you understand me.</i>

597
00:30:40,100 --> 00:30:42,200
[SAM]  I should just be
investigating him.

598
00:30:45,967 --> 00:30:47,900
<i>I should be taking
this opportunity</i>

599
00:30:47,900 --> 00:30:49,600
<i> to find out the truth.</i>

600
00:30:50,400 --> 00:30:52,867
<i>I'm becoming closer to him
than expected.</i>

601
00:30:54,600 --> 00:30:56,933
<i>I really want to help
and protect him.</i>

602
00:30:56,933 --> 00:31:03,867
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

603
00:31:21,367 --> 00:31:26,333
<i>I will do everything
to get out of this hellscape.</i>

604
00:31:26,333 --> 00:31:29,200
I got it. Just like I promised.

605
00:31:29,200 --> 00:31:32,000
<i>Won't you tell the neighbors
that you sold them off?</i>

606
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:34,433
<i>You need to wear
something decent and formal.</i>

607
00:31:34,433 --> 00:31:36,533
<i> And you need to cut your hair.</i>

608
00:31:36,533 --> 00:31:38,500
<i> But this is my strength.</i>

609
00:31:38,500 --> 00:31:41,033
<i>My sex appeal
comes from this hairstyle.</i>

610
00:31:41,033 --> 00:31:42,433
<i> What's Umali doing here?</i>

611
00:31:42,467 --> 00:31:43,733
<i>- I know this guy!
- You do?</i>

612
00:31:43,733 --> 00:31:45,333
<i>They're looking for that guy
they saw last night.</i>

613
00:31:45,333 --> 00:31:48,100
<i>And I'll make sure
it's Gabo that they find.</i>
